## Knowledge Check

### Question 1

A company wants each Job Application to be associated with one Position, while allowing each Position to have many Job Applications.

Where should the relationship field be created?

A. Position

B. Both objects

C. Job Application ✅

D. Junction Object

**Answer:** C

---

### Question 2

Why are relationship fields used?

A. Improve Apex performance

B. Associate objects so users can access related data ✅

C. Replace validation rules

D. Automatically enforce security

**Answer:** B

---

### Question 3

Which relationship type allows parent and child records to exist independently?

A. Master-Detail

B. Hierarchical

C. Lookup ✅

D. Many-to-Many

**Answer:** C

---

### Question 4

Which statement correctly describes a one-to-many relationship?

A. One child references many parents.

B. One parent can have many child records. ✅

C. Every parent must have a child.

D. The relationship field is created on the parent.

**Answer:** B

---

### Question 5

What is one of the primary purposes of Schema Builder?

A. Automatically create relationships.

B. Visualize objects and their relationships. ✅

C. Generate Apex classes.

D. Replace Object Manager.

**Answer:** B

---

## Key Takeaways

- Relationships connect Salesforce objects.
- Relationship fields are always created on the child object.
- One parent can have many child records.
- Lookup is a loosely coupled relationship.
- Schema Builder helps visualize the Salesforce data model.
